        "targetText": "3. Identify the scalar norm defectFor every scalar observable u, root energy equals ⟨(I−T²)u,u⟩. Selfadjointness of the same T gives ⟨T²u,u⟩=‖Tu‖²; thus ‖Γu‖²=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². The anonymous actual-input Test also checks ‖Γu‖≤‖u‖. This is a scalar B.11 precursor. Printed joint ΓP still requires the same onto M, restriction to ran(P) and the typed B*B identity; no full-space inverse is claimed.‖Γu‖2=‖u‖2−‖Tu‖2,‖Γu‖≤‖u‖.Corresponding Lean stephEnergy; hTs.isSymmetric; hs; real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq",
